        "original_id": "732cf091-cb85-5d24-8f10-44dd5fcec326",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Cutcliffe\n- Organizations: Duke Blue Devils football team, Ole Miss Rebels football team, Walter Camp Football Foundation, Maxwell Football Club, Bobby Dodd Foundation\n- Places: Wallace Wade Stadium, Durham, North Carolina, Vaught–Hemingway Stadium, Oxford, Mississippi, Independence Stadium, Shreveport, Louisiana\n- Events: 2002 Independence Bowl\n- Topics: college football coach of the year awards\n\nFacts:\n- On December 27, 2002, the 2002 Independence Bowl was a postseason college football bowl game between the Nebraska Cornhuskers and the Ole Miss Rebels at Independence Stadium in Shreveport, Louisiana.\n- In 2002, David Cutcliffe coached the Ole Miss Rebels football team, which played its home games at Vaught–Hemingway Stadium in Oxford, Mississippi.\n- In 2013, David Cutcliffe was in his sixth year as head coach of the Duke Blue Devils football team, which played its home games at Wallace Wade Stadium in Durham, North Carolina.\n- David Cutcliffe earned multiple college football coach of the year awards from the Walter Camp Football Foundation, the Maxwell Football Club, and the Bobby Dodd Foundation.",
